@@ -67,14 +67,57 @@ ## User Administration
 
 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+### Queue
+
+A queue belongs to **one entity**. It has:
+
+- A `name`.
+- A `slug`, unique within the entity.
+- An `is_active` flag (default `true`). Tickets can only be issued into an active queue.
+- Optional localized labels (`labels_i18n`, JSON), used by the web interface and totem API.
+
+Implementation: `App\Models\Queue`, with `entity()` and `tickets()` relations.
+
 ### Ticket
 
-Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
+Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call**. Attributes:
 
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
-- Priority (numeric, see below).
-- Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
-- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- Display `code` — per-queue sequence `A001`, `A002`, … (prefix `A`, at least 3 digits, zero padded; it simply grows beyond `A999`: `A1000`, `A1001`). Unique per `(queue_id, code)`.
+- Priority (integer, see below).
+- Issuance timestamp (`issued_at`; ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
+- Issuance channel: `totem`, `virtual` or `printed`.
+- Status: `waiting` or `called` (there is no cancelled status).
+- Call data: `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (nullable until called).
+
+Implementation: `App\Models\Ticket`, with `queue()` and `calledBy()` relations and the `TicketStatus`/`TicketChannel` enums.
+
+**Display code allocation:** the next code is the last valid code in insertion order plus one (not string order: `A999` → `A1000` → `A1001`). Malformed legacy codes (anything not matching `A<digits>`) are skipped, so `A001` followed by `A-X` yields `A002`, while only `A-X` yields `A001`. Deleting a ticket does not reuse its number: a per-queue high-water mark preserves the sequence even when the latest ticket is deleted (`A001`..`A003` with `A002` deleted → `A004`; deleting `A003` also yields `A004`).
+
+**Write-once:** after issuance every field is immutable except `status`, `called_at`, `called_by_user_id` (and `updated_at`). Any Eloquent save/update changing another field throws `LogicException`.
+
+### Issuance
+
+Issuance is performed by the invokable `App\Actions\IssueTicket`:
+
+```php
+$ticket = (new IssueTicket)($queue, $priority, TicketChannel::Virtual);
+```
+
+- The queue must be **active**. Its state is read and locked from the database inside the transaction, so a queue deactivated after the caller loaded it is still rejected; an inactive queue throws `App\Exceptions\InactiveQueueException` and persists nothing.
+- Priority is an integer `>= 0` (default `0`); a negative value throws `InvalidArgumentException`.
+- New tickets are `waiting`, `issued_at = now()`, channel `virtual` (unless given) and priority `0` (unless given).
+- The display code is allocated by the queue sequence. A unique `(queue_id, code)` collision from concurrent issuance is retried a few times.
+
+### Calling
+
+A ticket is called through `Ticket::call(User $user)`:
+
+- It can be called **exactly once**, marking it `called` and recording `called_at` and the calling user.
+- Only members of the ticket's entity may call it; anyone else gets `Illuminate\Auth\Access\AuthorizationException` and the ticket is unchanged.
+- Calling a ticket that is not `waiting` throws `LogicException`.
+
+Selection of *which* waiting ticket to call next (priority, age and fairness) is not part of the issuance/calling core yet.
 
 ### Priority
 
